<urn:atm:triage:finding/AI11-BLOCKING-02-HTTP-CONTRACT-GENERIC>
  a triage:Finding ;
  triage:findingId "AI11-BLOCKING-02-HTTP-CONTRACT-GENERIC" ;
  triage:foundIn triage:AICH-Legacy ;
  triage:foundAt "2026-07-21T00:00:00Z"^^xsd:dateTime ;
  triage:title "HTTP response always status 200; missing detail/read routes documented in OpenAPI" ;
  triage:description "Post-merge audit of integrate/phase-AI (quality-mgr + qa-triage independent confirmation). Two defects in HTTP API contract enforcement: (1) write_http_response (crates/atm-core/src/api.rs:107-114) hardcodes literal 'HTTP/1.1 200 OK' regardless of envelope content/error state, contradicting openapi.yaml documented 200/201/204 statuses and error-response handling contract. (2) ApiRequest::matches_route (api.rs:264-284) has no matching case for GET /v1/atm/message/{id} detail route or /v1/atm/message/{id}/read route, despite both documented in openapi.yaml. Note: /v1/atm/teams route removal is already an accepted waiver (openapi_surface_reviewed_removals.json); this finding addresses only the missing detail/read routes and always-200 status bug, which are NOT in that allowlist. Sprint-ai-9.md Deliverable 2 requires HTTP API contract parity with OpenAPI spec." ;
  triage:phaseId "phase-AI" ;
  triage:triageMode "initial_pass" ;
  triage:category "api-contract-violation" ;
  triage:severity "blocking" ;
  triage:repeatable true ;
  triage:sweepScope "crate" ;
  triage:status "fixed" ;
  triage:dispatchReady true ;
  triage:hasOccurrence <urn:atm:triage:occurrence/AI11-BLOCKING-02/pAI-11/1>, <urn:atm:triage:occurrence/AI11-BLOCKING-02/pAI-11/2> ;
  triage:triagedAt "2026-07-21T00:00:00Z"^^xsd:dateTime ;
  triage:reviewedBy "qa-triage", "quality-mgr" ;
  triage:notes "Post-merge audit finding (quality-mgr reconciliation 2026-07-26). Scope: crates/atm-core/src/api.rs (response encoding, request routing). Issue 1 (hardcoded 200 OK): FIXED -- write_http_response_body now derives status/reason from encode_response() rather than a literal 'HTTP/1.1 200 OK'. Issue 2 (/message/{id} missing routes): RESOLVED -- routes /message/{messageId} and /message/{messageId}/read are explicitly listed in crates/atm/tests/openapi_surface_reviewed_removals.json as intentionally reviewed and removed endpoints, NOT undocumented gaps. Finding premise predates intentional removal review. Both issues closed." .

